      "message": "administrivia: hashes are notoriously very fragile when not protected by a lock. Who is protecting this? I assume rt_mutex_lock(\u0026uid_lock), but will let you tell me ;-\u003e. The comment for the synchronization primitive needs to be updated to list this as protected, unless it is protecting this entire uid_entry structure. Am I right to assume this is the case?\n\nThankfully uid_lock is global, otherwise my concern would be that this list could be unprotected (even momentarily) because each pid (tgid) and tid can set its own uid individually/asynchronously.",
