      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the comment! Currently all read/write on task_entries are followed immediately after a read/write on the uid_entry it belongs to, since the invariant is each field of the tids, such as wchar rchar etc, needs to add up to the same value as the matching field in uid. So the sequence of read/write is: uid1, tid1.1, tid1.2, tid1.3, and/or uid2, tid2.1, tid2.2, ... Since each uid_entry struct is protected, task_entry structs should also be. I also checked each task_entries hash table to make sure that it lies inside the uid_lock.",
