      "writtenOn": "2017-07-28T19:32:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so reason there could be trailing spaces is because cmdline arguments could be set to null bytes in https://googleplex-android-review.git.corp.google.com/#/c/544666/ In the AndroidRuntime.cpp file, in the function setArgv0, argv0 is set entirely to zero at first and then the first several bytes are set to a readable name. And in the previous loop every null byte is converted to whitespace. So multiple unreasonable whitespaces could only appear at the end of args. The content before the multiple spaces should be intentionally written that way, for example \"system_server\".\n\nIf nothing is available except for the first at most TASK_COMM_LEN bytes for thread name. Variable i would be TASK_COMM_LEN at the start of this loop. And we would remove the trailing spaces forced in TASK_COMM_LEN as well :)",
